        ":question/id": "f2ec7bb2-2b5c-5a6c-af77-21a3068576a7",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-25124",
        ":question/problem": "Find the exact solution of the equation $3^{x - 2} = 6$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we take $\\log_3$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3^{x-2}&=6\\\\\n\\log_3\\left(3^{x-2}\\right)&=\\log_3(6).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ gives $x-2=\\log_3(6)$. Adding $2$ to both sides, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=\\log_3(6)+2.\n$$"
      }
